{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development would create a dwelling with an inadqeautely size bedroom (bedroom no.2), inaccessible skylights within both bedrooms and one small balcony which would only be accesible via a bedroom. As such this would creare a&nbsp;substandard quality of accommodation, and as such, would be unacceptable, contrary to:-&nbsp;DCLG Technical Housing Standards (nationally described space standard) (DCLG, March 2015) (as amended)Policy D6 and Table 3.1 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policies BP5 and BP6 of the Local Development Framework (LDF) Borough Wide Development Plan Document (DPD) (March 2011)Part 6 of policy DMNE1 of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan 2037: (Regulation 19 Submission Version, December 2021)",
    "The proposed change of use from the rear of commercial unit (Use Class E) to residential unit (Use Class C3) would result in the loss of floorspace for a commercial unit which sits within a neighbourhood centre, and the development fails to demonstrate a need for this facility in this location, the development is deemed to be unacceptable and contrary to:·&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Paragraph 93 of the National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (DLUHC, September 2023)Policy E9 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policies CM1 and CE1 Local Development Framework (LDF) Core Strategy (July 2010)Policies BE1 and BE2 of the Local Development Framework (LDF) Borough Wide Development Plan Document (DPD) (March 2011)Policies DME3 and DME5 of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan 2037: (Regulation 19 Submission Version, December 2021)",
    "The proposed development by reason of its scale, bulk, height, represents poor design, failing to respect the architectural design of the surrounding area, lacks articulation and interest and would not fit in with the character of the area, contrary to:Paragraphs 131 and 135 of the National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (DLUHC, September 2023)Policies D1 and D4 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy CP3 of the Local Development Framework (LDF) Core Strategy (July 2010)Policy BP11 of the Local Development Framework (LDF) Borough Wide Development Plan Document (DPD) (March 2011)Policies SP2, DMD1, DMD6 of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan 2037: (Regulation 19 Submission Version, December 2021)",
    "The proposed development by reason of its scale and siting would result in a loss of outlook, privacy and overbearing impact for neighbouring dwellings especially nos.10 St Chad&#39;s Road and 110a and 110b High Road. As such, the proposed development would have an unneighbourly impact and is deemed to be unacceptable.Part D of policy D6 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policies BP8 and BP11 of the Local Development Framework (LDF) Borough Wide Development Plan Document (DPD) (March 2011)Policy DMD1 of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan 2037: (Regulation 19 Submission Version, December 2021)"
  ],
